Subject: [PATCH] media: BMediaRecorder starts the producer it records from

Recording apps (R Sound Editor, R Spectrum) connected to the sound card's
input without error and then received no buffers at all.

The hda driver was fine: record interrupts arrived and the record buffer
cycle advanced. MultiAudioNode sends record buffers only while its run
state is B_STARTED, and it was B_STOPPED. Nobody starts it as a producer:
the media_server starts the mixer (which drives playback on its own), and
BMediaRecorder::Start() started only the node's time source when the node
is one - which a sound card's node always is - and the node itself only
otherwise.

Start the producer in either case. Starting a node that already runs is
harmless.

Verified on arm64 under QEMU (intel-hda + hda-duplex): a recorder that
got 0 buffers in 3 s now gets 16 per second, 393,216 bytes each second at
96 kHz, 2 channels, 16 bit.

diff --git a/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp b/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
index b4227875a1..e427379858 100644
--- a/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,15 @@ BMediaRecorder::Start(bool force)
 	if ((fOutputNode.kind & B_TIME_SOURCE) != 0)
 		err = BMediaRoster::CurrentRoster()->StartTimeSource(
 			fOutputNode, BTimeSource::RealTime());
-	else
+
+	// A sound card's node is its own time source and also the producer we
+	// record from. Starting only the time source leaves the producer in
+	// B_STOPPED, and MultiAudioNode sends record buffers only while started:
+	// the recorder connects fine and then never receives a single buffer.
+	// Nothing else starts it (the media_server starts the mixer, which starts
+	// playback on its own), so start the producer here. Starting a node that
+	// already runs is harmless.
+	if (err == B_OK && (fOutputNode.kind & B_BUFFER_PRODUCER) != 0)
 		err = BMediaRoster::CurrentRoster()->StartNode(
 			fOutputNode, fNode->TimeSource()->Now());
 
